<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Marj Dabiq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1516</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-mamluk-war-1516-1517">Ottoman–Mamluk War (1516–1517)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Marj Dabiq was fought in 1516 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selim-i">Selim I</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> army was decisively defeated and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> al-Ghawri was killed. Together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-conquest-of-egypt">Ottoman conquest of Egypt</a> in 1517, the battle marked the formal end of Mamluk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marj-dabiq.jpg" alt="Battle of Marj Dabiq" width="253" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Şükr-i Bitlisi (Yaşam süresi: 1531) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercidab%C4%B1k_Muharebesi2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
